# External Resource Credentials

When accessing resources outside Cursor (Jira, GitHub, Jenkins, Konflux, GitLab, Slack, Gemini, etc.), load credentials from:

`<workspace-root>/workflows/cve-service/config/.env`

(Replace `<workspace-root>` with the absolute path to the repo root on your machine, e.g. `/home/user/multicluster-global-hub-ai-agent`.)

Do not guess or ask for tokens. Source this file in shell commands or read it before API calls:

```bash
set -a
source <workspace-root>/workflows/cve-service/config/.env
set +a
```

Use the corresponding env vars (e.g. `JIRA_*`, `GITHUB_TOKEN`, `JENKINS_*`, `KONFLUX_TOKEN`, `GITLAB_*`, `SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL`, `GEMINI_*`).

`JIRA_EMAIL` must match your Atlassian account email exactly. A typo breaks API create/comment.

When creating ACM Jira issues, follow `skills/jira-create/SKILL.md` — always set **Component**, **Activity Type**, **Severity**, and **Priority**.

Never print, commit, or echo secret values from this file.
